  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">K&amp;I for Peace, Security and Justice</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(1) building a robust evidence base to support project acquisition and advocacy;  

(2) Prioritizing people-centered approaches by advancing with innovative programming, such as Results-Based Financing (RBF);  

(3) enhancing internal expertise in conflict sensitivity; and  

(4) integrating cross-cutting themes such as climate justice and locally led development.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Direct beneficiaries Cordaid staff</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Within Peace, Security, and Justice (PSJ) Cordaid is dedicated to enhancing security and justice systems in fragile and conflict-affected settings (FCAS) through innovative, evidence-based approaches. This proposal for the Knowledge &amp; Innovation Fund aims to strengthen Cordaid&#x2019;s internal capacities, refine our programming methodologies across the cycle (from conceptualization/design to implementational &amp; learning), and solidify our positioning with donors and external stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
